=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a Makefile that builds is production, so its edit reaches the weakened test as evidence, which the rule refuses (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case build_makefile_stays_prod_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: the discriminator is content, not the filename — a C build recipe is
origin2: real repair evidence for a test that changed with it, and demoting it
origin3: to ci would have invented false positives in every extension project.
=== before: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O1

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== after: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O2

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== before: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) == 7
=== after: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) > 0
